  "faq": {
    "title": "Frequently Asked Questions",
    "searchPlaceholder": "Search questions...",
    "noResults": "No results found",
    "q1": "How to use CubeVisage in Minecraft Bedrock Edition?",
    "a1": "■ Method 1\n1. Locate the downloaded CubeVisage UI zip file\n2. Long press the file or right-click and select 'Open with' (or 'Share resource pack')\n3. Select Minecraft\n4. In-game, go to Settings > Global Resources > CubeVisage UI > Activate\n5. Exit settings screen to load the resource pack\n\n■ Method 2\n1. First, locate the downloaded CubeVisage UI zip file\n2. Place the file in the appropriate directory:\nWindows: %localappdata%\\Packages\\Microsoft.MinecraftUWP_8wekyb3d8bbwe\\LocalState\\games\\com.mojang\\resource_packs\nAndroid/HarmonyOS: Android/data/com.mojang.minecraftpe/files/games/com.mojang/resource_packs\nThen in-game go to Settings > Global Resources > CubeVisage UI > Activate\nIOS: My Device > Minecraft > games > com.mojang > resource_packs\n\n* com.mojang.minecraftpe is the package name, if using different package please locate accordingly",
    "q2": "How to import resource packs in Minecraft Java Edition?",
    "a2": "1. Place the resource pack .zip file in .minecraft/resourcepacks folder\n2. Launch Minecraft\n3. Go to Options > Resource Packs\n4. Enable the desired resource pack",
    "q3": "Is CubeVisage UI 26 and above versions good to use?",
    "a3": "CubeVisage UI 26 and above versions use the Frost River Engine for a smoother experience. More features have been added to optimize gameplay, making it lighter and better to use!",
    "q4": "How to disable or remove Ore UI?",
    "a4": "[Learn more at https://openlist.endyun.ltd](https://openlist.endyun.ltd)",
    "q5": "What versions does CubeVisage UI support?",
    "a5": "- Bedrock Edition: 1.8 and above\n- Java Edition: 1.21.5 and above\n- Bedrock Ore UI Edition: Corresponding version (marked in downloaded filename)",
    "q6": "How to use extensions?",
    "a6": "Same import method as CubeVisage UI. After activation, pay attention to resource pack order:\nExtensions > CubeVisage UI",
    "q7": "How to customize UI?",
    "a7": "[Visit customization page](/custom)\nCustom packs should be ordered above CubeVisage UI",
    "q8": "How to enable CubeVisage Panel?",
    "a8": "Load the CubeVisage Panel extension pack. Two ways to access:\n1. In pause screen, double-click settings button at bottom left\n2. For touch users, click toolbox left of hotbar, then click settings button on right",
    "q9": "Why are CubeVisage Panel settings reset?",
    "a9": "This is because switch states are stored temporarily. Switching worlds or dimensions will reset them. You can change default settings at [customization page](/custom)",
    "q10": "How to enable chunk map?",
    "a10": "Import and activate Chunk Map extension pack, then enter world to see it\n\nIf CubeVisage Panel is enabled, you need to enable chunk map in panel settings, or set it to default on at Customize > Panel > Chunk Map\n\nAlso chunk map requires coordinate display, enable at Settings > World > Show Coordinates",
    "q11": "Can I modify it?",
    "a11": "It is forbidden to modify, decompile and crack the resource package. See the latest version of user agreement for details. Users are only allowed to change the configuration through custom websites",
    "q12": "What is a zip file?",
    "a12": "A zip file is a compressed archive that contains one or more files combined into a single file for easier storage and distribution. It uses compression to reduce file size while preserving all the original data when extracted"
  },
